sentences.text:
Accordingly, in the event of arrest the respondentsState Authorities shall release the petitioner on bail, subject to the observance of following conditions:
(i) RespondentState Authorities shall release bail petitioner [Jitender Kataik] on bail on furnishing personal bond of Rs.75,000/ {Rs. Seventy Five Thousand} with one surety of the like amount to the satisfaction of the Investigating Officer;
(ii) Petitioner shall appear before the Investigating Officer or SHO, Police Station concerned on 11.02.2025 at 03.00 p.m. and an subsequent dates thereafter;
(iii) Petitioner shall undertake and shall appear on every date of trial hereinafter;
(iv) Petitioner shall abide by all or any other condition(s), which may be imposed by the Investigating Officer concerned, in view of this order;
(v) Petitioner shall neither involve himself nor shall abet the commission of any offence hereinafter.

(vii) Petitioner shall not jump over the bail and shall not leave the country without the prior information of the Court;
Jitender Kataik vs . State Of H.P. on 10 February, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/69867009/
2 (viii) Petitioner shall not tamper with the evidence in any manner;
(ix) Petitioner is free to seek modification of any condition contained hereinabove, if need arises;
(x) State Authorities are free to move this Court for seeking alteration/modification of any of the condition contained in this order or any condition imposed by Investigating Officer concerned as a sequel to this order, is fact situation or circumstances so necessitate, at any time hereinafter;
(xi) State Authorities are free to move this Court for seeking cancellation of concession of bail, in case, the petitioner violates any condition(s) contained in this order hereinafter;
13. Petitioner is permitted to produce/use copy of this order, downloaded from the webpage of the High Court of Himachal Pradesh, before the authorities concerned, and the said authorities shall not insist for production of a certified copy, but if required, may verify passing of order from Website of the High Court.
14.

